# Domain 5 — Session 24: Autonomous Agent Risk Matrix

## 1. Scenario Description

The AI application is an autonomous customer-support agent powered by a large language model (LLM). It can read customer messages, retrieve customer records, create support tickets, send emails, and issue refunds within a configured limit. It interacts with external APIs and uses stored conversation history to make decisions.

Although these capabilities improve efficiency, they introduce security risks because the agent can access sensitive information and perform actions that affect customers and the organization. Security controls must ensure that the agent follows authorized instructions, accesses only permitted data, and performs actions within defined limits.

